  <details class="legend">
    <summary>Rules &amp; payouts</summary>
    <ul>
      <li><b>Blackjack</b> — a natural 21 on your first two cards. Pays {{ blackjackOdds.blackjackPayoutStr }}, unless the dealer also has one (push).</li>
      <li><b>Dealer</b> — stands on all totals of 17, including soft 17. Peeks for blackjack immediately when showing an Ace or a 10-value card, before you act.</li>
      <li><b>Double down</b> — double your bet and take exactly one more card, on any first two cards, including after a split.</li>
      <li><b>Split</b> — split a matching-rank pair into two hands of equal bet. One split per hand, no resplitting. Split aces get exactly one card each and can't be hit again.</li>
      <li><b>Insurance</b> — offered only when the dealer shows an Ace. Costs half your bet, pays {{ blackjackOdds.insurancePayoutStr }} if the dealer has blackjack. A bet against your own hand, not for it — the math favors the house here, same as any insurance bet.</li>
      <li><b>Push</b> — a tie returns your bet with no win or loss.</li>
      <li><b>Shoe</b> — dealt from a real 6-deck shoe, reshuffled between hands once it runs low.</li>
    </ul>
  </details>

  <p>
    Blackjack is a race to 21 without going over, played against the dealer alone —
    other players at a real table don't affect your hand. Every decision comes down
    to the same math: hit, stand, double, or split based on your total against the
    dealer's up-card.
  </p>

  <p class="strategy-link"><a href="/strategy/blackjack/">Read the blackjack rules and strategy guide →</a></p>
